{
  "_createdAt": "2026-04-27T18:27:04Z",
  "_id": "wp-post-153058-en",
  "_rev": "Kra5TYIFOKLIQlRCd8I5t5",
  "_type": "article",
  "_updatedAt": "2026-07-05T16:14:44Z",
  "author": {
    "_ref": "author-legacy-archive",
    "_type": "reference"
  },
  "body": [
    {
      "_key": "000000000001",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000000",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "What matters in an Egypt travel package is not only the price. It is how the trip is built."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000003",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "2r1513t0sdq6",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The "
        },
        {
          "_key": "vnthli28z4wg",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "herzql6o13dz"
          ],
          "text": "Giza"
        },
        {
          "_key": "fxzl9dloag8g",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " pyramids, "
        },
        {
          "_key": "uprfbklvjij6",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "wqwy301ia07w"
          ],
          "text": "Luxor"
        },
        {
          "_key": "ds82x2nz3zn9",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "'s temples, "
        },
        {
          "_key": "xq86zecubcqw",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "sqpdxqoyzmjn"
          ],
          "text": "Aswan"
        },
        {
          "_key": "7v6j1um3gvnv",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "_key": "n06lcpvw4gb5",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "1uzpbhf7pmc8"
          ],
          "text": "Abu Simbel"
        },
        {
          "_key": "nfy92kfna1a9",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", the Red Sea. Looking only at the names tempts you to put them all in. Egypt is a large country. "
        },
        {
          "_key": "k6qzxvdpy4sz",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "k7kh9vlozqdl"
          ],
          "text": "Cairo"
        },
        {
          "_key": "ct7wtpf3rogl",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " and Luxor are not close. Abu Simbel is further again from Aswan. The Red Sea is a different trip from the Nile valley."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "herzql6o13dz",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-58854",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        },
        {
          "_key": "wqwy301ia07w",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-58877",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        },
        {
          "_key": "sqpdxqoyzmjn",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-58758",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        },
        {
          "_key": "1uzpbhf7pmc8",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-56813",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        },
        {
          "_key": "k7kh9vlozqdl",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-83284",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        }
      ],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000005",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000004",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "A good package does not list sights. It orders the transfers, sets the nights, holds rest time, sources good guides, and chooses boats and hotels well. A package that is only cheap loses time and stamina on the ground."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000007",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000006",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "In Egypt, the design of the itinerary is itself the value."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000009",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000008",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The basic route"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000000b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000000a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The most natural shape for a first Egypt trip enters via Cairo and runs to Luxor and Aswan."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000000d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000000c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Cairo and Giza: pyramids, the Grand Egyptian Museum, Saqqara, the Islamic quarter, the Coptic quarter. The doorway. Looking only at the pyramids and flying south makes the line of the Old Kingdom and Cairo's depth as a city hard to see."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000000f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "6e6hx5qhur67",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Luxor is the centre of an ancient-Egypt trip. Karnak, "
        },
        {
          "_key": "b6twi92ihq5i",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "kkz2oiulv9cd"
          ],
          "text": "Luxor Temple"
        },
        {
          "_key": "rs6r2ik4rij6",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", the "
        },
        {
          "_key": "yw24kcecug6g",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "6zfi8p9bgn1j"
          ],
          "text": "Valley of the Kings"
        },
        {
          "_key": "jt5sk4tpu35v",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", Hatshepsut, "
        },
        {
          "_key": "yvikzs12aocq",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "qt80irewk746"
          ],
          "text": "Medinet Habu"
        },
        {
          "_key": "y5riejnf263g",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ". Packages that do it in a day rush. At least two nights, ideally three, gives room to split east and west banks."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "kkz2oiulv9cd",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "guideArticle.luxor.the-luxor-temple",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        },
        {
          "_key": "6zfi8p9bgn1j",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "guideArticle.luxor.valley-of-the-kings",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        },
        {
          "_key": "qt80irewk746",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "guideArticle.luxor.madinat-habu-temple",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        }
      ],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000011",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "xbjwbtiy9fha",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Aswan slows the pace a little. Philae, "
        },
        {
          "_key": "hbm9dglaqst7",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "nnrhx0fmcdc4"
          ],
          "text": "the Unfinished Obelisk"
        },
        {
          "_key": "zhbplag3snu3",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", Nubian culture, the Nile islands, and the gateway to Abu Simbel. A different Egypt from Luxor — don't make it a pass-through."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "nnrhx0fmcdc4",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "guideArticle.aswan.the-unfinished-obelisk",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        }
      ],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000013",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "ehotnrmvtpk9",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "With these three at the spine, a first Egypt trip stands up solidly. The Red Sea and "
        },
        {
          "_key": "vx5bamw6wlm7",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "syknx7b1o17a"
          ],
          "text": "Alexandria"
        },
        {
          "_key": "js2b6769g8x7",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " are additions for when days allow."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "syknx7b1o17a",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-58750",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        }
      ],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000015",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000014",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "How many days"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000017",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000016",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "For a first Egypt visit, packages of seven days or fewer are tightly focused trips. Cairo and Luxor only, or Cairo and the Red Sea only, are possible; saying you saw the whole country is harder."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000019",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000018",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Eight to ten days lets you run Cairo, Giza, Luxor, and Aswan once. Transfers add up. Including Abu Simbel asks for early mornings and margin."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000001b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000001a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Ten to twelve days becomes quite stable as a first trip. Two or three nights in Cairo, two or three in Luxor, several at Aswan or on the Nile cruise. You can add a short Red Sea here too."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000001d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000001c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Twelve to fourteen days changes how Egypt reads. Cairo without rushing, the Luxor west bank in depth, rest in Aswan, the Red Sea at the end to recover. The trip becomes a flow, not a check-off."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000001f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000001e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "When looking at packages, look not only at the day count but at where you actually sleep how many nights. An \"eight-day\" trip that includes arrival and departure can leave only six days of real movement on the ground."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000021",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000020",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Packages with a Nile cruise"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000023",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "pak1e8yus6hl",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Nile cruises are one of the most common shapes in Egypt packages. Moving by boat between Luxor and Aswan, visiting "
        },
        {
          "_key": "4v3jpgugngk6",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "0vb563dlspnb"
          ],
          "text": "Edfu"
        },
        {
          "_key": "jqyp2k89vrad",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "_key": "gqep60136kie",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "ggb1prnpsqou"
          ],
          "text": "Kom Ombo"
        },
        {
          "_key": "5cqyyg0gmlji",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "_key": "rpppa6jym2au",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "ehciqtf4rzuk"
          ],
          "text": "Esna"
        },
        {
          "_key": "ytcdv2psoguf",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "0vb563dlspnb",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-58841",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        },
        {
          "_key": "ggb1prnpsqou",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-58875",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        },
        {
          "_key": "ehciqtf4rzuk",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-58844",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        }
      ],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000025",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000024",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The cruise's advantage is movement and lodging in one. Not changing hotels each day and seeing the temples on the way efficiently. Practical for first trips."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000027",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000026",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The experience shifts heavily with boat quality and guide quality. A \"5-star cruise\" does not necessarily mean the same as an international 5-star hotel. Confirm cabin condition, food, boat age, stops, guide, and sightseeing time."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000029",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000028",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Large ships are efficient and time-locked. For a quieter Nile, dahabiya packages exist. Small sailing-style cruises, slower pace, closer to the river. Higher price, with real value for travellers who want the Nile as the trip's lead."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000002b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000002a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Packages that add the Red Sea"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000002d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "5msb9zsh157e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "If the Red Sea is in, the end of the trip works. After Cairo, Luxor, and Aswan in history, rest at "
        },
        {
          "_key": "pe68v2f257cd",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "crxxwl0dyrlq"
          ],
          "text": "Hurghada"
        },
        {
          "_key": "zbg1e9dcrm2d",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", Sharm el-Sheikh, or Marsa Alam."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "crxxwl0dyrlq",
          "_type": "internalLink",
          "reference": {
            "_ref": "wp-page-58859",
            "_type": "reference"
          }
        }
      ],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000002f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000002e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Hurghada is the Red Sea base easiest to combine with Luxor. Three and a half to four hours each way by road, mainland-side and comparatively legible. Packages that add Luxor sites to a beach stay often use it."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000031",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000030",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Sharm el-Sheikh is the Sinai-side resort. Strong for Ras Mohammed and Strait of Tiran diving; connections to Cairo and Luxor need careful judgement."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000033",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000032",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "A single Red Sea night in a package often does not earn its place. Transfer, check-in, and check-out eat the time. To add the sea, two nights minimum, ideally three, for it to function as rest."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000035",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000034",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Looking at a cheap package"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000037",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000036",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Egypt has very cheap packages. Cheap itself isn't bad. Season, hotel occupancy, flights, and exchange rates can land on a good price."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000039",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000038",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The question is what has been cut."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000003b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000003a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "First, hotel location. A \"Giza hotel\" is not necessarily close to the pyramids. A \"Cairo hotel\" may not be convenient for sightseeing flow. In Luxor, east vs. west bank changes transfers. On the Red Sea, distance from the airport and ease of getting into the sea matter."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000003d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000003c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Second, the guide. Egyptian sites change with explanation quality. Packages with no guide or only shallow explanation can look cheap and miss the value."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000003f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000003e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Third, entry fees. Confirm whether main-site tickets, separate-ticket tombs, museums, Abu Simbel, and on-cruise visits are included. Cheap packages can stack on-the-ground extras."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000041",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000040",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Fourth, transfers. Private car or shared? Domestic flight or long-distance bus? Sleeper train? Transfer quality maps directly to fatigue."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000043",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000042",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "If you pick a cheap package, do it with the cuts understood."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000045",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000044",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Looking at an expensive package"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000047",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000046",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Expensive doesn't automatically mean good. Lining up luxury hotels with a too-rushed schedule is possible."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000049",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000048",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "What to look for is margin. Is there time at the Cairo museums? Is the Luxor west bank given more than a day? Is Aswan not just for sleeping? Does the Red Sea have nights you can actually rest in?"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000004b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000004a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Then specialisation. Who is the guide? How can they explain the GEM, Saqqara, the Valley of the Kings, Karnak? Are the dahabiya or cruise boat names clear? If they advertise special access or private visits, what is actually included?"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000004d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000004c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The value of a high-end package shows in time and arrangement quality more than in hotel rank. Morning entries that avoid crowds, transfers without strain, good guides, afternoons to rest. Without those, it is only expensive."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000004f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000004e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Guided or independent"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000051",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000050",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "You can do Egypt independently. With flights, hotels, domestic flights, and ride-hailing, the major-city movement is possible. Experienced travellers can build their own."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000053",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000052",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Explanation matters greatly for the sites. At the Valley of the Kings, Karnak, Saqqara, Abu Simbel, and the GEM, what you can read without a guide is limited. Wall paintings, gods, royal names, the orientation of architecture, the difference between tomb and temple don't read off the ground naturally."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000055",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000054",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The best middle is putting a specialist guide on the important visits while spending evenings and free time on your own. You don't need to do everything in a group. You don't need to do everything alone either."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000057",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000056",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "A good package balances this. Use specialisation where sightseeing needs it; leave free time open. The trip doesn't go rigid."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000059",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000058",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Family packages"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000005b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000005a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "For family travel, don't pack the schedule. Pyramids, mummies, boats, desert, and the Red Sea are strong for children — heat, early starts, and long transfers stack into fatigue."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000005d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000005c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "For family travel, Cairo and Giza, Luxor, and the Red Sea often work well in combination. Adding Aswan and Abu Simbel needs days. With small children, the early-morning Abu Simbel transfer is a real question of fit."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000005f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000005e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "For hotels, confirm room size, connecting rooms, pool, food flexibility, and airport distance. On the Red Sea, kids' clubs and the presence of shallow sea also matter."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000061",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000060",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "In a family package, the value is daily-good-mood movement, not the number of sites."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000063",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000062",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Couples and honeymoon packages"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000065",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000064",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "For couples and honeymoons, slow the trip. Egypt is romantic; rushed, it becomes a trip of transfers and early starts only."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000067",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000066",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "See pyramids and museums in Cairo, see temples and tombs in Luxor, take a dahabiya slowly on the Nile, close with the Red Sea. That flow suits a honeymoon."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000069",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000068",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "For hotels, prize view and quiet. Pyramid view at Giza, Nile view at Luxor and Aswan, adult-oriented quiet resorts on the Red Sea. Staying longer at good places beats moving each night to a new luxury hotel."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000006b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000006a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Packages by season"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000006d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000006c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The best season for Egypt is generally October to April. Cairo, Luxor, and Aswan walk well and Nile cruises run smoothly."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000006f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000006e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "December to January is popular and prices rise. Lock in hotels, boats, and guides early. November, February, and March balance weather and crowds."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000071",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000070",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "May to September is hot. Luxor and Aswan especially need attention to daytime sightseeing. Prices can drop, and the Red Sea works as a sea trip. A summer package needs early-morning sightseeing, midday rest, and seaside stays in its design."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000073",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000072",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Ramadan, religious feasts, and Egyptian holiday periods also shift the trip. Dates change year to year — confirm before booking."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000075",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000074",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Conditions of a good package"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000077",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000076",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "A good Egypt package shares a few traits."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000079",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000078",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Cairo not rushed."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000007b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000007a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Enough time in Luxor."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000007d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000007c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Aswan not only a transit."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000007f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000007e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "A clearly named Nile cruise or dahabiya with clear content."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000081",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000080",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Guide quality described."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000083",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000082",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "If the Red Sea is in, nights that allow real rest."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000085",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000084",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Add-on fees that are legible."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000087",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000086",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Hot-season time allocation that is realistic."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000089",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000088",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "With these, even a mid-priced package can run as a good trip. Without them, cheap or expensive both produce problems."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000008b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000008a",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Conclusion"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000008d",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000008c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Egypt package travel is, built well, a very strong shape. The country is large, the sites are spread, the transfers are many, and good design earns its value."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "00000000008f",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "00000000008e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "A package is not an assortment of sights. From Cairo south, from the Old Kingdom to the New, from the Nile to the Red Sea. The order matters."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "000000000091",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000090",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "A good Egypt package does not rush you. It arranges not only what you see, but how you see it."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    }
  ],
